#
# bg_scroll.checks - one row per CHECK of fixtures/src/bg_scroll.s (D-125, plan 04-12). Columns separated by one TAB: check index (1-based), slug, class tag, meaning.
# Class tags: MAN:<page> (a manual page value; the page label must be in fixtures/lib/cites.txt), GUEST:<model>, ASSUMED:<LED-id>.
# Every check here is a readback of what the guest wrote, compared with an expectation the guest forms by a different computation than the writer (the tiles against the ROM table they were uploaded from, the palette against an additive sum), so it holds under every power-on policy (D-167).
# The raster, the scroll latch and the wrap are judged from the line records by the video cases (fixtures/src/bg_scroll.vexp), not here. A pass is not a support claim (ER-4).
id=23
checks=4
1	tile-low-bytes	GUEST:tile-readback	The low bytes of the 64 tile words read back through VRR equal the ROM table the block upload took them from
2	tile-high-bytes	GUEST:tile-readback	The high bytes of the 64 tile words equal the ROM table
3	pal-low-sum	GUEST:pal-bijection	The 512 palette entry low bytes equal the additive running sum E(i + 1) = (E(i) + 91) & 511 from E(0) = 17, a different computation from the multiplicative writer
4	pal-bit8-sum	GUEST:pal-bijection	The 512 palette entry bit 8 values equal the same running sum
